==Trivia==
*Farmer Cat was designed by IKU, the winner of the [[PONOS Campaigns/The Next Battle Cats Design Contest|Cat Design Contest]] in 2017. She was later made obtainable as a stamp reward from 12/22/17 to 12/31/17.
**The results of "The Next Battle Cat - Design Contest" are located [https://ponos.s3.amazonaws.com/information/appli/battlecats/news/en/charadesign_2017.html here].
**She is the second cat to be designed by a fan, [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]] being the first.
*During the [[Anniversary/6th Year|6th]] and [[Anniversary/7th Year|7th anniversary]] events, Farmer Cat became available as the 3rd stamp reward.
*Harvest Cat's description may be referencing the Stalk Market in the ''[[wikipedia:Animal Crossing|Animal Crossing]]'' series of games.
*Harvest Cat may also be a reference to [[wikia:rhythmheaven:Rhythm Heaven|''Rhythm Heaven'']]'s [[wikia:rhythmheaven:Stomp Farmer|Stomp Farmer]], who pulls turnips out of the ground in a similar fashion.
*Not counting [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]], Farmer Cat was the first unit to ''gain'' the ability to upgrade to + levels.
*While the Japanese names of Farmer Cat and [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] can both be translated as "Cat Farmer", they aren't exactly the same, as they use different words to say "Farmer". Farmer Cat uses 農家 ''nōka'' (the Japanese word for farmer), while Farmboy Cat uses ファーマー ''fāmā'' (a transliteration of the English word ''farmer'').
*In the French translation of [[The Battle Cats]], Farmer Cat and [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] are both named "Chagriculteur", a portmanteau of ''chat'' (cat) and ''agriculteur'' (farmer).

